                                     rdfs:subClassOf <http://w3id.org/aqfo/aqfo_00002330> ;
                                     obo:IAO_0000115 "Red vent syndrome is an inflammation of the fish’s anal orifice (or anal vent). The inflammation of the anus region is associated with the presence, and especially an unusually high concentration, of the parasite Anisakis simplex in the tissues surrounding the anus."@en ;
