###  http://w3id.org/aqfo/aqfo_00000021
<http://w3id.org/aqfo/aqfo_00000021> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                     rdfs:subClassOf <http://w3id.org/aqfo/aqfo_00002010> ;
                                     obo:IAO_0000115 "The amount of fishing gear of a specific type used on the fishing grounds over a given unit of time (e.g. hours trawled per day, number of hooks set per day, or number of hauls of a beach seine per day) to be used to compare catch rates in the same fishery. When two or more kinds of gear are used, the respective efforts must be adjusted to some standard type before being added. Sometimes referred to as effective fishing effort. Across different fisheries or gear types, a standardised unit of effort must be used, such as time fishing per vessel or person (e.g. fisher days)." ;
                                     dc:creator <http://orcid.org/0000-0002-2789-1558> ;
                                     dcterms:creator <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6363-0945> ;
                                     rdfs:label "fishing effort" .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://w3id.org/aqfo/aqfo_00000021> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty obo:IAO_0000115 ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "The amount of fishing gear of a specific type used on the fishing grounds over a given unit of time (e.g. hours trawled per day, number of hooks set per day, or number of hauls of a beach seine per day) to be used to compare catch rates in the same fishery. When two or more kinds of gear are used, the respective efforts must be adjusted to some standard type before being added. Sometimes referred to as effective fishing effort. Across different fisheries or gear types, a standardised unit of effort must be used, such as time fishing per vessel or person (e.g. fisher days)." ;
   oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Blackhart, K., Stanton, D. G., & Shimada, A. M. (2006). NOAA fisheries glossary (Revised edition). Silver Spring, MD: United States Department of Commerce, National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration.;https://spo.nmfs.noaa.gov/sites/default/files/tm69.pdf"
 ] .


