###  http://w3id.org/aqfo/aqfo_00002012
<http://w3id.org/aqfo/aqfo_00002012> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                     rdfs:subClassOf <http://w3id.org/aqfo/aqfo_00002000> ;
                                     obo:IAO_0000115 """The network of firms that bring products to market, from companies that produce raw materials to retailers and others that deliver finished products to consumers. Economic value is added through the coordinated management of the flow of physical goods and associated information at each stage of the chain.

A value chain is the entire series of activities and transactions needed to make a product and deliver it to consumers. A value chain is a key concept to understand agri-food system economics and development. It considers all the stakeholders that intervene and interact in food production and consumption. It shows the links between different activities and economic sectors.""" ;
                                     dc:creator <http://orcid.org/0000-0002-8461-9745> ;
                                     dcterms:creator <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4169-2456> ;
                                     oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "supply chain" ;
                                     rdfs:label "value chain" .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://w3id.org/aqfo/aqfo_00002012> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty obo:IAO_0000115 ;
   owl:annotatedTarget """The network of firms that bring products to market, from companies that produce raw materials to retailers and others that deliver finished products to consumers. Economic value is added through the coordinated management of the flow of physical goods and associated information at each stage of the chain.

A value chain is the entire series of activities and transactions needed to make a product and deliver it to consumers. A value chain is a key concept to understand agri-food system economics and development. It considers all the stakeholders that intervene and interact in food production and consumption. It shows the links between different activities and economic sectors.""" ;
   oboInOwl:hasDbXref """U.S. Department of Agriculture. (n.d.). NAL Agricultural Thesaurus and Glossary. Beltsville, MD: U.S.D.A. 

Agrilinks.org
;https://agclass.nal.usda.gov/mtwdk.exe?k=glossary&l=60&w=14631&s=5&t=2

https://www.agrilinks.org/post/what-value-chain-example-aquaculture"""
 ] .


