###  http://w3id.org/aqfo/aqfo_00002067
<http://w3id.org/aqfo/aqfo_00002067> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                     rdfs:subClassOf <http://w3id.org/aqfo/aqfo_00002018> ;
                                     obo:IAO_0000115 "Is a marker that could be used in digestibility studies in animals as an alternative to the total collection method. It consists of indigestible mineral components, mainly silica. Acid-insoluble ash contents of feeds and faeces are determined gravimetrically after drying, ashing, boiling of ash in hydrochloric acid (HCl), filtering and washing of the hot hydrolysate, and re-ashing." ;
                                     dc:creator <http://orcid.org/0000-0002-8461-9745> ;
                                     rdfs:label "acid insoluble ash" .

