   owl:annotatedSource <http://w3id.org/aqfo/aqfo_00002067> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty obo:IAO_0000115 ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "Is a marker that could be used in digestibility studies in animals as an alternative to the total collection method. It consists of indigestible mineral components, mainly silica. Acid-insoluble ash contents of feeds and faeces are determined gravimetrically after drying, ashing, boiling of ash in hydrochloric acid (HCl), filtering and washing of the hot hydrolysate, and re-ashing." ;
   oboInOwl:hasDbXref "Sales, J., & Janssens, G. P. J. (2003). Acid-insoluble ash as a marker in digestibility studies: a review. Journal of Animal and Feed Sciences, 12(3), 383-401.;"
 ] .


